$ patslint
stderr: usage: patslint [option | file] ...
stderr:
stderr: Check the style of ATS source files (.sats, .dats, .hats).
stderr:
stderr: options (an option applies to the files that follow it):
stderr:   -h, --help           print this help
stderr:   --list-rules         print the rules and their default severities
stderr:   --enable=RULE,...    turn rules on (at their default severity)
stderr:   --disable=RULE,...   turn rules off
stderr:   --severity=RULE:SEV  set the severity of a rule
stderr:                        (off, info, warning, error)
stderr:   --max-col=N          the maximal length of a line (default 80)
stderr:   --indent-width=N     the unit of indentation (default 2)
stderr:   --lines=N-M,...      report only the findings on these lines
stderr:   --all-lines          report the findings on all the lines (default)
stderr:   --fail-on=SEV        the least severity that makes the exit status 1
stderr:                        (default warning)
stderr:   --format=text|json   the output: one finding per line, text or JSON
stderr:   --source             (text) each finding is followed by its line and
stderr:                        a caret under its column (the default when the
stderr:                        output is a terminal)
stderr:   --no-source          (text) the findings only
stderr:   --fix                fix trailing-ws, crlf, final-newline, blank-eof
stderr:                        and the tabs of indentations in place
stderr:   --semantic           also the rules after the binding of the names
stderr:                        (unused-var, ...; slower: the prelude is loaded)
stderr:
stderr: The nearest .patslint file in the directory of a file or above it
stderr: configures its check (lines of the form KEY = VALUE, # for comments):
stderr:   RULE = off | on | info | warning | error
stderr:   max-col = N
stderr:   indent-width = N
stderr:   exclude = GLOB       (relative to the directory of .patslint)
stderr: The options of the command line take precedence over it.
stderr: A comment [lint: disable=RULE,...] disables rules on its line and the
stderr: next one, [lint: disable-file=RULE,...] in the whole file (RULE can
stderr: be [all]).
exit: 2
